title: The Health Service Dispute
tags: event
view-if: con_in_government = 1 and time >= 52 and time <= 56 and health_dispute = 0 and (nhs_contracting = 1 or union_power >= 50 or nhs_funding = 0 or nupe_mood >= 70)
max-visits: 1
new-page: true
on-arrival: health_dispute = 1; strike_wave += 2

= The Health Service Dispute

Nurses, porters and ancillary staff have rejected a pay offer of between 4% and 6%. [? if nhs_contracting = 1 : The health unions are already angry about contracting out, and the porters and cleaners are leading the action. ?] There are rolling one-day strikes across the country, and the TUC calls a "day of action" in support. The nurses' own college refuses to strike, but the public is on their side.

- @hold: Hold the line: no more money outside the cash limits.
- @nurses: Pay the nurses more, and hold the line for the rest.
- @settle: Settle with everyone.

@hold
subtitle: Union power falls if we win. A long and unpopular dispute.
on-arrival: union_power -= 4; strike_wave += 1; thatcher_rating -= 2; nupe_mood += 15; tuc_mood += 5; de_con -= 2; c2_con -= 1; dry_dissent -= 3; wet_dissent += 4

The dispute drags on for months, with emergency cover only in many hospitals. In the end the unions accept a two-year deal close to the original offer. They have been beaten, and they won't forget it.

@nurses
subtitle: -1 budget. Divides the strikers.
on-arrival: budget -= 1; union_power -= 2; strike_wave -= 1; c1_con += 1*(1-dissent); de_con += 1*(1-dissent); wet_dissent -= 2; nupe_mood += 5

The nurses get a pay review body of their own and a better offer, and their support for the dispute ebbs away. The ancillary workers fight on alone, and lose.

@settle
subtitle: -2 budget. Peace in the hospitals; the dries call it surrender.
on-arrival: budget -= 2; union_power += 3; strike_wave -= 2; de_con += 1*(1-dissent); wet_dissent -= 4; dry_dissent += 6; economic_liberalism -= 1; nupe_mood -= 15

The money is found from the contingency reserve. The hospitals return to normal, and other public-sector unions start drafting their claims.
